So yeah, that's quite a lot! While there are things we've missed, we're sure you'll have fun planning the beginning of your route around this new start and we've notified Civitas illa Fortis to be prepared for the flood of new arrivals and they've helped us prepare:
* Your auto-completed quests will mean instant access to:
** Fairy Rings & Zanaris
** Cam Torum & The Moons of Peril
** Vardorvis
* You can train Slayer instantly by speaking with Chaeldar in Zanaris. All Slayer Masters will assign you the same tasks, taking into account the areas you have currently unlocked.
* Agility can be trained from level 1 with the new stones around Yama's Lair and gives similar XP rates to Draynor Village Rooftop Course, so should bridge the gap between 1 and the Wyrm Agility Course. This course works slightly differently to others, so get ready to get hotfooted!
* Some shops have expanded their wares:
** The Elemental shield and Anti-dragon shield have been added to all Slayer Equipment shops
** Bronze, Iron & Steel daggers and Halberds have been added to the Fortis Blacksmith
** Box traps & Bird snares have been added to the Fortis General Store
** Bronze, Iron & Steel Knives have been added to Arcuani's Archery Supplies in Tal Teklan
** Hunting crossbow at the Sunset Coast charter ship just like the previous league
* For those who are unaware, you can use the Bank in the Hunter's Guild before completing At First Light
* Some creatures such as cows & Hill Giants will respawn more frequently to help with the influx of players to the region

